{"id":"2-me-dmt","name":"2-Me-DMT","form":"spray","status":"Documented","aliases":"","category":"Psychedelic","summarySources":"TripSit","summary":"Also known as 2,N,N-TMT, this drug was first synthesised by Alexander Shulgin. Described as a very mild psychedelic of similar subjective effects to other tryptamines. Reported as having an unusual and unpredictable dose curve, it is recommended to start low with this drug.","doseMaxTick":200,"doseUnit":"mg","doseRows":[{"roa":"Oral","source":"TripSit","unit":"mg","light":"30–50 mg","common":"50–75 mg","strong":"75–100 mg","heavy":"100 mg+","commonEstimate":63,"band":{"low":50,"high":75},"domain":[24,165],"segments":{"light":[30,50],"common":[50,75],"strong":[75,100],"heavy":[100,158.4]}}],"durationSources":"TripSit","durationRows":[{"roa":"Oral","onset":"60–90 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–5 h","total":"3–8 h"},{"roa":"Insufflated","onset":"15–40 min","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–5 h","total":"3–8 h"},{"roa":"General","onset":"—","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"1–5 h","total":"3–8 h"}],"subjectiveEffects":[{"name":"Euphoria"},{"name":"Empathy"},{"name":"Insight"},{"name":"Brightened colour"},{"name":"Closed/Open eye visuals"},{"name":"Enhanced tactile sensation"},{"name":"Mental/physical stimulation"},{"name":"Decreased appetite"},{"name":"Pupil dilation"},{"name":"Restlessness"},{"name":"Change in perception"},{"name":"Ego softening"},{"name":"Sweating/chills"},{"name":"Muscle tension"},{"name":"Confusion"},{"name":"Insomnia"}],"combinations":[],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/2-me-dmt"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_2MeDMT.shtml"},{"title":"TiHKAL Entry","description":"Alexander & Ann Shulgin tryptamine monograph","url":"https://www.erowid.org/library/books_online/tihkal/tihkal34.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2-Methyl-DMT"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on 2-Me-DMT","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4596816"}],"wikidata":"Q4596816","pharmacology":{"text":"Its affinities (Ki) for the serotonin 5-HT1A and 5-HT2A receptor were 4,598 nM and 15,037 nM, respectively. These affinities were dramatically lower than those of dimethyltryptamine (DMT) in the same study, which were 87 nM and 1,513 nM, respectively. Hence, 2-methyl-DMT appears to show approximately 53- and 10-fold lower affinities for the serotonin 5-HT1A and 5-HT2A receptors compared to DMT.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"2-Methyl-DMT","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2-Methyl-DMT#Pharmacodynamics"},"uses":{"routes":"Oral","figures":"2-Methyl-DMT"}}